     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day, and 1,700 mg is also more than the usual maximum single dose (1,000 mg for immediate-release). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose or formulation.** An example is extended-release, which is usually given once daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you meant, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
